   484	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   485	// Arm 1 — the repro
   486	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   487	
   488	/// **TC-90 REPRO ARM (TC-57-shaped, paced).** A loop of `Engine::transition` calls
   489	/// against a live projection worker.
   490	///
   491	/// **MEASURED 0/20 at `94f09d7d`** (two sessions of 10) — 120 transitions,
   492	/// 122-147 competing writes,
   493	/// ~175 embeds per run. This arm does NOT reproduce TC-90; the stress arm does.
   494	/// It is kept because it is the arm directly comparable to TC-57's, and because a
   495	/// fix must keep it green.
   496	///
   497	/// `#[ignore]`d for the same reason TC-57's pair was: this is a characterization
   498	/// instrument whose baseline result is a MEASUREMENT, not a merge-gate invariant,
   499	/// and `cargo test --workspace` is not a stable signal for concurrency tests
