dev/plans/runs/codex/0.8.20/slice-22-fix-1-rereview-20260729T011134Z.log:2954:The test at [tc68_probe_fingerprint_cache.rs:681](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s22/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/tests/tc68_probe_fingerprint_cache.rs:681) proves that an attacker who can rewrite all 45 `_fathomdb_embed_probe.reference_vec` blobs to the target drifted backend’s exact outputs can defeat the full probe. It does not prove that this is equivalent in capability or cost to writing one cached digest row. The cache-marker attack only needs DB write access plus the current digest, which may already be stored or publicly computable. The baseline attack additionally requires producing the target backend’s 45 exact probe embeddings and encoding/updating every row correctly. That is a materially higher bar.
