   498	### 5.3 (a) The baseline duplicate rate — MEASURED, both arms
   499	
   500	**Definition of "duplicate" used throughout:** every row this fixture writes carries a **unique**
   501	body, and the embedder records the exact `text` of every `embed()` call. `ingest_duplicates` is
   502	the number of embed calls **beyond the first** for any single text. A text embedded twice is a
   503	row that was dispatched twice — i.e. a projection outcome that was computed and then never
   504	became durable. This is a count, not an inference from a total.
   505	
   506	Protocol: 200 single-row `Engine::write` calls 1 ms apart, live 1 ms embedder, `doc` enrolled as
   507	a vector kind, `drain`, then count. N = 10 per arm.
   508	
   509	```bash
   510	for arm in tc91_duplicate_embed_rate_governed tc91_duplicate_embed_rate_anonymous; do
