   158	  rc=$?
   159	  if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then f=$((f+1)); fi
   160	done
   161	echo "STRESS CONTROL FAILURES: $f/10"
   162	```
   163	
   164	**Paced pair** (N = 10 each) — substitute
   165	`tc90_repro_transition_loop_races_projection_worker` and
   166	`tc90_control_transition_loop_without_second_writer` into the same loop.
   167	
   168	`rc=$?` is on the line immediately after the command in every loop. Anything between them —
   169	**including a command substitution** — silently reports *that* command's status instead
   170	(TC-57 §1.1: this invalidated a verification in this repo).
   171	
   172	**Do NOT** measure through `cargo test --workspace` (TC-72) or `scripts/agent-test.sh` (its
   173	aggregate exit is vacuous — it aborts at the known-red actionlint fixture long before the Rust
   174	step).
   175	
   176	### 2.2 Measured results at `94f09d7d`
   177	
   178	Two independent sessions of 10 runs per arm — the second run after the assertions were tightened
   179	(§2.1). **Every arm replicated exactly.**
   180	
   181	| arm | writers × burst | write pace | embed delay | vector kind | runs | failed |
   182	|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
   183	| paced repro | 1 × 1 | 3 ms | 2 ms | yes | 20 | **0/20** |
   184	| paced control | 1 × 1 | 3 ms | 2 ms | **no** | 20 | **0/20** |
   185	| **stress repro** | 2 × 24 | 1 ms | **0 ms** | yes | 20 | **20/20** |
   186	| stress control | 2 × 24 | 1 ms | 0 ms | **no** | 20 | **0/20** |
   187	
   188	Stress repro detail, per run — `EngineError::Storage` failures out of 40 transitions. **Two
   189	independent measurement sessions**, the second run after the assertions were tightened:
   190	
   191	| session | per-run storage errors | mean | rate |
   192	|---|---|---|---|
   193	| A (first draft) | 3, 4, 10, 3, 6, 6, 5, 5, 8, 9 | **5.9** | 14.8 % |
   194	| B (tightened assertions) | 8, 4, 4, 1, 4, 2, 4, 4, 3, 4 | **3.8** | 9.5 % |
   195	| **pooled (N = 20)** | **1 – 10** | **4.9** | **12.1 %** |
   196	
   197	**Read the reproduction rate, not the failure rate.** The arm reproduced **10/10 in both
   198	sessions** — that is the stable, load-bearing result. The *per-run count* is not stable across
   199	sessions (mean 5.9 vs 3.8 on the same machine, same commit, same arm), so **quote it as a range,
   200	1–10 failures per 40 transitions (≈ 2.5 %–25 %), not as "14.8 %".** §4's bar is written against
   201	the reproduction rate for exactly this reason.
   202	
   203	In **all 20** runs across both sessions: `attempted == 40`, `truncated == false`,
   204	`scheduler_errors == 0`, `other_errors == 0` — so the signal is the promote race and nothing
   205	else, and (since session B) that is asserted rather than merely reported. The first failure
   206	landed as early as index **0** and as late as index **20**; the failing call returned in
   207	**9–84 ms**, essentially all of which is its own `drain`. Competing writes per run: 2280–2952.
   208	Embeds per run: 6353–9612.
   209	
   210	Stress control: `embed_calls == 0`, 1920–1968 competing writes, **0 storage errors in all 20
   211	runs across both sessions**. The load alone does not break `transition`.
   212	
   213	Paced repro: 120 transitions, 122–147 competing writes, 132–202 embeds, **0 failures**, 20/20.
   214	Paced control: 120 transitions, 41 competing writes, `embed_calls == 0`, **0 failures**, 20/20.
   215	
   216	### 2.3 What the arms hold constant
   217	
   218	Within each pairing the **only** difference is `Engine::configure_vector_kind_for_test("doc")`
   219	— i.e. whether the projection worker ever produces a `Success` outcome and therefore whether a
   220	**second writer exists at all**. Embedder, seed rows, competing-write threads, burst size,
   221	pacing, transition loop and subject set are identical. This is the same isolation TC-57 §4.2
   222	performed.
   223	
   224	**Non-vacuity, both directions.** Every arm asserts the state of its own independent variable
   225	rather than assuming it: repro arms assert `embed_calls > 0` (a second writer *did* exist),
   226	control arms assert `embed_calls == 0` (it did *not*), and all four run
   227	`assert_protocol_ran` (§2.1) for the rest. A run in which the worker never ran cannot report a
   228	clean pass for the wrong reason; a control that silently lost its load cannot masquerade as a
   229	clean comparison; and an arm that measured 1 transition instead of 40, or spent the run in drain
   230	timeouts, now fails instead of passing quietly.
   231	
   232	**One harness detail that is load-bearing, not cosmetic.** The loop tracks each subject's state
   233	from **observed outcomes**, never from the loop index. A failed `transition` rolls back, so the
   234	subject keeps its previous state; deriving the next target from the index would then aim a flip
   235	at the state the row is already in — a self-loop, correctly refused with `IllegalTransition`.
   236	That refusal is a **cascade artifact of the harness**, and in the first draft of this
   237	measurement it contaminated the very counter under test (an early run reported
   238	`storage_errors=1 other_errors=1`, where the second was pure artifact). Advancing only on
   239	success removes it; `other_error_kinds` is reported so a future recurrence is visible rather
   240	than silent.

